From ec37e51d0627e776c3f9e6d0a8fbba197f2d5ca5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:03:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: the PIC32CM MC00 temperature sensor (TSENS U2261)

mchp-tsens-u2261 converts as two probe rounds on MC00 rev A1 silicon
showed (firmware/hello APP=tsensprobe, tsensprobe2): (2 GAIN + 2000)
GCLK_TSENS periods per conversion, GAIN = 0 counting as 2^24, and
VALUE = OFFSET + GAIN * D(T) / f_GCLK with D(T) from the part's factory
calibration, so firmware loading it reads the "temperature" property in
hundredths of a degree. START and the START event are ignored while
converting or disabled; a conversion waits for its GCLK; disabling
aborts, but one that FREERUN started runs again at the next enable.
OVERRUN on an unread result, OVF beyond 24 bits, the signed window
monitor with a WINMON event pulse per match, SWRST keeping GAIN, OFFSET,
CAL and DBGCTRL. qtest pic32cm-tsens-test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
